cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "hillcreep: hillslope diffusivity built from a creep velocity profile"
abstract: >-
  Evolves a soil-mantled hillslope between two rivers, with the transport
  coefficient assembled rather than assumed. Downslope soil velocity decays
  exponentially below the land-air interface; integrating that profile over the
  mobile layer gives the depth-integrated flux and, with it, a hillslope
  diffusivity D = K H*, the product of the surface creep velocity at unit slope
  and the e-folding depth of the motion. D is reported as a consequence of two
  measurable quantities rather than set as a parameter, and the velocity field
  it summarises is drawn beneath the hillslope. Built for teaching, and
  delivered as an interactive browser demo.
type: software
